This file gathers and re-exports the basic vocabulary of Scott's section 2 on LAMBDA, combinators, and the first recursion theorem: terms, the combinatory predicate and combinatory expressions, minimal and maximal extension, the conditional set, environment update, interpretation, occurrence and renaming, binary and ternary currying, finite Scott continuity, finite currying and nested application, the omega and Y combinators, the sequence constructors, relational composition and set sum, top recursion, combinatory interpretation, abstraction and erasure, the subspace of graphs, sequence cons, the intersection step and combinator, sequence functions, the dollar combinator and its shift and step, the bounded sequence function, omega abstraction, primitive recursion, the parameterized fixed-point map, the closed Y term, term shift, the term forms of the dollar step and the primitive-recursion step, and membership in a numeral.
